CORE
main.c
--unwind 2 --rounds 2 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness --no-assertions --datarace
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
Negative control for `pthread_create_output_param_race`: two threads
correctly take turns through the same mutex around the same shared
variable. Confirms that narrowing `is_pthread` to exempt only
`pthread_create` did not also expose `pthread_mutex_lock`/`_unlock`'s own
internal state (owner/count/recursive) to false-positive races -- this must
stay SUCCESSFUL before and after the fix.
